  84:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *                                          CREATE A MESSAGE MAILBOX
  85:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *
  86:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** * Description: This function creates a message mailbox if free event control blocks are available.
  87:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *
  88:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** * Arguments  : pmsg          is a pointer to a message that you wish to deposit in the mailbox.  If
  89:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *                            you set this value to the NULL pointer (i.e. (void *)0) then the mailb
  90:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *                            will be considered empty.
  91:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *
  92:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** * Returns    : != (OS_EVENT *)0  is a pointer to the event control clock (OS_EVENT) associated with
  93:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *                                created mailbox
  94:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *              == (OS_EVENT *)0  if no event control blocks were available
  95:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
  96:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** */
