 500:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *
 501:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** * Description: This function sends a message to a mailbox
 502:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *
 503:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** * Arguments  : pevent        is a pointer to the event control block associated with the desired ma
 504:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *
 505:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *              pmsg          is a pointer to the message to send.  You MUST NOT send a NULL pointer
 506:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *
 507:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** * Returns    : OS_ERR_NONE          The call was successful and the message was sent
 508:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *              OS_ERR_MBOX_FULL     If the mailbox already contains a message.  You can can only se
 509:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *                                   message at a time and thus, the message MUST be consumed before
 510:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *                                   are allowed to send another one.
 511:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *              OS_ERR_EVENT_TYPE    If you are attempting to post to a non mailbox.
 512:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *              OS_ERR_PEVENT_NULL   If 'pevent' is a NULL pointer
 513:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *              OS_ERR_POST_NULL_PTR If you are attempting to post a NULL pointer
 514:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** *
 515:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** * Note(s)    : 1) HPT means Highest Priority Task
 516:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** ***************************************************************************************************
 517:./ucos/Core/os_mbox.c **** */
